A modular Python project analyzing the Titanic passenger dataset through data cleaning, exploratory data analysis, and visualization.  
The project investigates how factors such as gender, age group, embarkation port, and passenger class influenced survival rates during the Titanic disaster.

## Overview

This project was developed as an introduction to practical data analysis workflows in Python.

The original notebook-based analysis was progressively reorganized into a modular project structure, separating data loading, analysis logic, visualization, and execution workflow.

The project focuses on:

- Data loading and preprocessing with Pandas
- Exploratory data analysis on passenger survival patterns
- Survival rate comparison across demographic and ticket-related variables
- Automatic generation of visual outputs
- Modular Python code organization for reproducibility

---

## Features

- Modular Python project structure
- Data loading from a CSV dataset
- Survival analysis by:
  - Gender
  - Age group
  - Embarkation port
  - Passenger class
- Visualization of survival patterns with Matplotlib
- Automatically generated output charts
- English and French notebook reports for portfolio presentation
- Reproducible execution through `main.py`

---

## Technical Stack

- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Jupyter Notebook
- GitHub Codespaces / local Python environment

